m Treatment: A Meta-Analysis</article-title><source>Alcohol Clin Exp Res</source><volume>25</volume><fpage>1335</fpage><lpage>41</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11584154</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b25-ndt-2-445"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lesch</surname><given-names>OM</given-names></name><name><surname>Walter</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Subtypes of alcoholism and their role in therapy</article-title><source><italic>Alcohol</italic> Alcohol</source><volume>31</volume><issue>Suppl 1</issue><fpage>63</fpage><lpage>67</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8737003</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b26-ndt-2-445"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Littleton</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1995</year><article-title>Acamprosate in alcohol dependence: How does it work?</article-title><source>Addiction</source><volume>90</volume><fpage>1179</fpage><lpage>88</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7580816</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b27-ndt-2-445"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Littleton</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Zieglgansberger</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Pharmacological mechanisms of naltrexone and acamprosate in the prevention of relapse in alcohol dependence</article-title><source>Am J Addict</source><volume>12</volume><issue>Suppl 1</issue><fpage>S3</fpage><lpage>11</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14972776</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b28-ndt-2-445"><citation citation-type="web"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Mallinckrodt</collab></person-group><year>2005</year>RiVea (naltrexone hydrochloride) Tablets patient package insert [online]. Accessed on 21 October 2005. URL: <ext-link ex